{
  "//": [
    "Coverage verdicts ASH's own assess_coverage reaches, which src/coverage.ts must reproduce.",
    "",
    "Each case names a real results file under test/fixtures/scans/ (captured from `ash scan`",
    "and path-sanitized) and a list of [path, value] edits applied to a copy of it. Three suites",
    "read this file and must agree with it: test/coverage.test.ts runs src/coverage.ts,",
    "tests/unit/test_vscode_coverage_parity.py runs ASH's assess_coverage on the same",
    "edited documents, and the JetBrains plugin's AshCoverageParityTest runs AshScannerStatus.",
    "An edit to any implementation that moves a verdict fails one of them.",
    "",
    "`incomplete_scanners`, `incomplete_converters` and `stale_content_databases` list names",
    "only; the Python side reduces its payload to the same shape before comparing."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "base": "scans/findings/ash_aggregated_results.json",
      "expect": {
        "coverage_complete": true,
        "incomplete_converters": [],
        "incomplete_scanners": [],
        "no_scanner_ran": false,
        "stale_content_databases": [],
        "unevaluated_rules": []
      },
      "name": "real findings scan, exit 2, one result suppressed",
      "set": []
    },
    {
